commit fe75722c612a76e32bf8c2a0ad8fdeb02c7450c0
Author: Shabakebehdasht <Shabakebehdasht@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 17 09:16:32 2026 +0000

    perf: paginate the persons, todos and units report tables
    
    All three report pages built their row list with a bare `->get()` — no limit,
    no `paginate()` — then mapped every row to an array and emitted a `<tr>` for
    each. An account scoped to a whole ministry therefore hydrated, mapped and
    shipped every person / todo / unit in scope, and because all the filters are
    `wire:model.live` it did so again on every filter change, not just on load.
    
    Wrap the trait around the row list only: `->paginate($this->perPage)` with
    `perPage = 25`, mapped over the page's collection so `$p` keeps its model type.
    Every aggregate keeps running against its own unpaginated clone, so `total`,
    `byUnit`, `byTahsil`, `bySemat`, `byEstekhdam`, `byType`, `byDay`, `completed`
    and `pending` still describe the whole filtered set — paginating them would
    change what the report means.
    
    The payload keys the views and the fail-closed `ReportsEmptyScopeTest` treat as
    plain arrays (`persons` / `items` / `units`) stay plain arrays holding the
    current page; each paginator rides alongside under `...Paginator`. The
    hand-rolled tables have no `with-pagination`, so the control is rendered by
    hand and the app's own `mary-table-pagination` hook keeps the active page
    themed like every other paginated page.
    
    `getAccessibleUnitsProperty()` also drops to `get(['id', 'name'])`: it only
    populates a `<select>`.
    
    Closes #1024

 phpstan-baseline.neon                              |  20 +-
 resources/views/livewire/reports/persons.blade.php |  48 ++-
 resources/views/livewire/reports/todos.blade.php   |  47 ++-
 resources/views/livewire/reports/units.blade.php   |  41 ++-
 tests/Feature/ReportsPaginationTest.php            | 371 +++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 506 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)
=== DIFF ===
